1174	 * because the cost of getting it wrong is destroying a customer's data:
1175	 *
1176	 *   • TYPE=disk (a whole device, never a partition/LVM/crypt node),
1177	 *   • no FSTYPE on the device itself,
1178	 *   • no partitions or children of ANY kind carved out of it,
1179	 *   • no mountpoint anywhere in its tree (walked via PKNAME, so an LVM or
1180	 *     dm-crypt stack rooted on the disk still disqualifies it),
1181	 *   • it is not the disk carrying the root filesystem,
1182	 *   • `blkid` finds NO signature at all on it,
1183	 *   • nothing in /sys/block/<dev>/holders is using it,
1184	 *   • it is at least MIN_EXTRA_DISK_BYTES.
