1189	 * Returned largest-first, and ALL of them, so the caller can tell the customer
1190	 * honestly what is attached ("2 unused volumes, largest is 30 GB") even though
1191	 * only ONE is ever used — separate volumes are separate filesystems and the
1192	 * engine deliberately does not weld them together. Every name has passed
1193	 * BLOCKDEV_RE, so it is safe to interpolate into a command.
